variants length must be exactly {{ n_variants }}.
elements per variant must be exactly {{ n_elements }}.

subject is ALWAYS English and concrete: not “horror atmosphere”, but “old film projector”.
It goes straight into the image generator.

subject requirements:
- One clear object (or, if category=5 and gold enabled, 1–2 characters in a simple beat),
  readable silhouette. No abstraction.
- 3–8 English words naming the object + material/shape only.
- The silhouette must match what the card IS. Name and subject must agree.
- Prefer the distinctive shape of that object class (shield badge ≠ five-point star;
  rotary phone ≠ candy blob; dossier folder ≠ open box of toys).
- Do NOT put lighting recipes, shadows, atmosphere, palette hex, floor/table lectures,
  viewing-angle instructions, or “no characters” into subject — art.j2 owns those.
- Camera / binoculars / glasses ARE valid objects — describe the prop, not a photo.
- Bad: “brass lamp casting sharp shadows on wood, high-contrast lighting, noir atmosphere”
- Bad: “metallic star badge” for a detective badge (draws a candy star)
- Good: “brass banker desk lamp amber glass shade”
- Good: “gold detective shield badge with eagle crest”
- Good: “chrome field binoculars with dual lenses”
- Good: “vintage movie camera with twin film reels”

title_ru = what the player sees on the card: 1–2 words in the OUTPUT LANGUAGE
(field name is legacy; language follows OUTPUT LANGUAGE).
